Falsifies `printenv::proofs::the_buffer_can_be_filled_exactly`.

The defect: `push`'s guard reserves the last byte of the buffer (`*n + 1 < buf.len()`), as a
C programmer keeps a slot for a NUL. It is memory-safe, so `push_never_writes_past_the_buffer_it_was_given`
stays green, but no input fills the buffer any more and the `cover` goes unsatisfiable.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(n, core::cmp::min(CAP, start + bytes.len()))`. (The `cover` beside it goes unsatisfiable but does not turn Kani red; see the strengthening commit.)

